abstract: >
  Reproducibility bundle for the paper "Reduction of the Wagstaff Chebyshev
  sufficiency conjecture to the Single-Pass Conjecture" by Alexey Dolotov.
  For W_p = (2^p + 1)/3 and omega_3 = 3 + 2*sqrt(2), the congruence
  omega_3^{(W_p+1)/2} = -1 (mod W_p) (Condition II) holds for every prime
  W_p; whether it implies primality is the open Wagstaff Chebyshev
  sufficiency conjecture, the Chua-form counterpart of the Vrba-Reix Wagstaff
  primality test. Writing P_p for the set of primes r with ord_r(2) = 2p at
  which Condition (II) holds locally, the Single-Pass Conjecture (SPC)
  asserts |P_p| <= 1 for every prime p >= 5; the paper proves that SPC
  implies the sufficiency conjecture unconditionally, with zero computational
  inputs, and that the working chain PPPC + MPC^> + X1 (with the Platinum
  enumeration and the witness discharges as stated computational inputs)
  also suffices and is implied by SPC. Proved unconditionally along the way:
  NCT for every odd d <= 400 (28 fixed-d certificates in (100,400]) and a
  complete danger-triple census through d = 400. This bundle contains the
  LaTeX source (v4.0, with v3.8 archived), the reproducibility scripts, the
  static NCT fixed-d certificates and the danger-census artifact (pinned
  factorizations, APR-CL certified).
